This product implements a subset of the Attention Manifest Protocol (AMP v0.1)
as published by the `attention-manifest-protocol` npm package
(https://github.com/eloyhere/attention-manifest-protocol), Copyright 2026
Eloy Kim, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The protocol surface reused here is the Goal and Plan object model, AMP ids
(`^[a-z][a-z0-9._:-]{0,63}$`), `amp: "0.1"`-tagged objects, the lifecycle edge
tables, canonical JSON digests with `sha256:` prefixes, the append-only
`{seq, kind, payload, prev, hash}` chain and the exported `ledger-snapshot`.
`mcp/lib/amp.mjs` declares those primitives; `mcp/lib/store.mjs` builds and
verifies the chain and the snapshot; `mcp/lib/goals.mjs` and `plans.mjs` produce
the artifacts; `collaboration.mjs` records duties as an explicitly labelled host
projection rather than an AMP object kind. `docs/PROTOCOL.md` records what was
adopted, how it is verified against the reference implementation, and what is
deliberately not implemented.

The server has no third-party runtime dependencies: only Node.js built-in
modules (`node:crypto`, `node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:readline`) are imported.
